 ### [Gaussian Rasterization Key Generation](5133-gaussian-rasterization-key-generation.md)
-This method generates the key-value pairs required for the tile-based rasterization of 3D Gaussians. It maps each 3D Gaussian to every tile it overlaps, creating one work item per (Gaussian, tile) pair. The keys pack the tile ID and depth to enable a single global radix sort that simultaneously bins splats by tile and sorts them by depth. It differs from [Tile-Based Culling](2819-tile-based-culling.md) by generating explicit overlap entries rather than filtering, and from [Tile-based Depth Sorting](8038-tile-based-depth-sorting.md) by handling the key construction logic explicitly before the sort phase.
